<section class="page-intro wrap policy-intro" aria-labelledby="policy-title"><p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p><h1 id="policy-title">Made to work <span class="muted">for everyone.</span></h1><p class="lede">How solarityai.com is built and checked so that people can use it with a keyboard, a screen reader, zoom, or other assistive technology.</p></section>
{#- -#}
<section class="policy-body wrap" aria-label="Accessibility statement">
<div class="policy-section"><h2>Our standard</h2><p>We design and test this website to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p></div>
<div class="policy-section"><h2>How we check it</h2><ul>
<li>Automated axe-core checks of every page, at phone and desktop widths.</li>
<li>Keyboard-only navigation, with a visible focus outline on every link and control.</li>
<li>Text spacing and zoom checks, so content stays readable when text is enlarged or spaced out.</li>
<li>Reduced motion: with that setting on, every animation stops and the page is complete without it.</li>
<li>Windows high contrast and the increased-contrast setting are supported.</li>
<li>Icons are labelled, links that open a new tab say so, and screenshots have written descriptions.</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="policy-section"><h2>Known limitations</h2><ul>
<li>App screenshots are pictures of app screens. Their descriptions summarise each screen; small interface text inside them is not reproduced.</li>
<li>The app stores, our SaaS products, the booking calendar, the careers form provider, the Google Forms for feedback, mentorship, and certificates, and our social channels are separate sites with their own accessibility practices.</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="policy-section"><h2>Tell us about a problem</h2><p>If something on this website is hard to use, email <a href="mailto:{{ email }}?subject=Solarity%20AI%20%7C%20Accessibility">{{ email }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> with the page and what happened, and we will reply and fix what we can.</p></div>
</section>
